# agnos_emit_probe — exercises the AGNOS ring-3 ABI so `_agnos_emit_gate`
# (programs/checks/ts.cyr) can assert that `CYRIUS_TARGET_AGNOS=1` emits a valid
# agnos binary: a `write`(syscall 1) to stdout + a non-zero exit via the
# COMPILER's exit emission (EEXIT), so the gate verifies the agnos exit epilogue
# is `syscall(0)`, NOT Linux `60`/`0xB8 0x3C`, and a valid ELF64 at entry ≥
# 0x200000 (agnos's user-range floor). See CHANGELOG [6.0.49].
#
# PEER-INDEPENDENT BY DESIGN — do NOT `include "lib/syscalls.cyr"` here.
# This gate tests the COMPILER's exit emission, not the syscall peer. The
# no-Linux-60 check byte-scans the whole binary for `mov eax,60` (`B8 3C ...`),
# and **agnos legitimately has syscall #60 = `winsize`** (a real wrapper in the
# peer: `sys_winsize`). Pulling the peer in would put a legitimate `mov eax,60`
# (winsize) in the binary and false-positive this gate — which is exactly the
# v6.2.39 bug. Using only raw `syscall(...)` here keeps the EEXIT the sole
# possible source of `mov eax,60`, so the scan is precise. Peer wrapper emit
# (winsize #60 / net_config #61 / signals) is covered by
# scripts/agnos-crossbuild-gate.sh probe 1h.
fn main(): i64 {
    syscall(1, 1, "agnos-ok\n", 9);   # raw write(stdout) — agnos #1, no peer include
    return 42;                         # non-zero exit via the compiler's agnos EEXIT (syscall 0)
}
